ll,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that a missing/unverifiable remote-tracking tickets ref (never fetched) yields eligible=false without error, and add an AC covering the absent-ref case distinctly from the reachable-but-false case.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4763,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'checks the corresponding remote-tracking tickets ref ... returns true only when the checkpoint commit is an ancestor of that ref'","Plan item 4 forbids fetch, so the local remote-tracking ref may not exist at all","freshness.py:102 treats a missing remote ref via `rev-parse --verify` as 'never fetched — no basis', a defined branch the plan's ACs do not enumerate","G6 checklist 1: edge/empty/failure cases handled"],"finding":"The plan does not specify the predicate's behavior when the configured remote-tracking tickets ref is absent locally (never fetched) — a distinct case from 'reachable but false'. Since the plan forbids fetching, a fresh/partial clone may have no `refs/remotes/<sync.remote>/<tracker.branch>` at all; the mechanism must define this as ineligible (returns false) rather than crash on a rev-parse failure.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc6377a38bfbc3be5","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Implementation plan items 1 & 4; ACs for unreachability","norm_id":"n4955179c2a7fe86c","priority":0.1237,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A disposable/fresh shadow clone or CI checkout that has not fetched the tickets remote ref","The configured sync.remote or tracker.branch resolves to a ref that does not exist locally"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that `checkpoint_commit_eligible`/`retired_tombs